<h5 class=3D"ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Sampled MuZero</h5><button clas=
s=3D"sr-only button" style=3D"display: none;">Report issue for preceding el=
ement</button>
<div class=3D"ltx_para ltx_noindent" id=3D"S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1">
<p class=3D"ltx_p" id=3D"S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.5">Since the efficiency of MCTS=
 planning is intricately tied to the number of simulations performed, the a=
pplication of MuZero has traditionally been limited to domains with relativ=
ely small action spaces, which can be fully enumerated on each node during =
the tree search. To tackle larger action spaces,
Sampled MuZero&nbsp;<cite class=3D"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(Hubert et=
&nbsp;al., <a class=3D"ltx_ref" href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2405.11778v1=
#bib.bib21" title=3D"">2021</a>)</cite> introduces a sampling-based framewo=
rk where policy improvement and evaluation are computed over small subsets =
of sampled actions.
Specifically, every time in the <span class=3D"ltx_text ltx_font_italic" id=
=3D"S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.5.1">Expansion</span> stage, only a subset <math alt=
text=3D"T(s)" class=3D"ltx_Math" display=3D"inline" id=3D"S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p=
