<section class=3D"ltx_section" id=3D"S7">
<h2 class=3D"ltx_title ltx_title_section">
<span class=3D"ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">7 </span>Reproducibility</h2><butto=
n class=3D"sr-only button" style=3D"display: none;">Report issue for preced=
ing element</button>
<div class=3D"ltx_para ltx_noindent" id=3D"S7.p1">
<p class=3D"ltx_p" id=3D"S7.p1.1">We ensure the reproducibility of our rese=
arch by providing comprehensive information and resources that allow others=
 to replicate our findings.
All experimental settings in this paper are available in <a class=3D"ltx_re=
f" href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2405.11778v1#A2" title=3D"Appendix B Impl=
ementation Details =E2=80=A3 Efficient Multi-agent Reinforcement Learning b=
y Planning"><span class=3D"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span>&nbsp;<span=
 class=3D"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>, including details on environm=
ental setup, network structure, training procedures, hyperparameters, and m=
ore.
The source code utilized in our experiments along with clear instructions o=
n how to reproduce our results will be made available upon finalization of =
the camera-ready version.
The benchmark employed in this investigation is either publicly accessible =
or can be obtained by contacting the appropriate data providers.
Additionally, detailed derivations for our theoretical claims can be found =
in <a class=3D"ltx_ref" href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2405.11778v1#A7" tit=
le=3D"Appendix G Derivation of AWPO Loss =E2=80=A3 Efficient Multi-agent Re=
inforcement Learning by Planning"><span class=3D"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appe=
ndix</span>&nbsp;<span class=3D"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G</span></a>.
We are dedicated to addressing any concerns or inquiries related to reprodu=
cibility and are open to collaborating with others to further validate and =
verify our findings.</p><button class=3D"sr-only button" style=3D"display: =
none;">Report issue for preceding element</button>
</div>
