<section class=3D"ltx_paragraph" id=3D"A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2">
<h5 class=3D"ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Combining reinforcement learnin=
g and planning algorithms</h5><button class=3D"sr-only button" style=3D"dis=
play: none;">Report issue for preceding element</button>
<div class=3D"ltx_para ltx_noindent" id=3D"A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1">
<p class=3D"ltx_p" id=3D"A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1">The integration of reinforce=
ment learning and planning within a common paradigm has yielded superhuman =
performance in diverse domains&nbsp;<cite class=3D"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_c=
itep">(Tesauro, <a class=3D"ltx_ref" href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2405.11=
778v1#bib.bib50" title=3D"">1994</a>; Silver et&nbsp;al., <a class=3D"ltx_r=
ef" href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2405.11778v1#bib.bib44" title=3D"">2017<=
/a>; Anthony et&nbsp;al., <a class=3D"ltx_ref" href=3D"https://arxiv.org/ht=
ml/2405.11778v1#bib.bib2" title=3D"">2017</a>; Silver et&nbsp;al., <a class=
=3D"ltx_ref" href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2405.11778v1#bib.bib45" title=
=3D"">2018</a>; Schrittwieser et&nbsp;al., <a class=3D"ltx_ref" href=3D"htt=
ps://arxiv.org/html/2405.11778v1#bib.bib42" title=3D"">2020</a>; Brown et&n=
bsp;al., <a class=3D"ltx_ref" href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2405.11778v1#b=
ib.bib7" title=3D"">2020</a>)</cite>. In this approach, RL acquires knowled=
ge through the learning of value and policy networks, which in turn guide t=
he planning process. Simultaneously, planning generates expert targets that=
 facilitate RL training. For example, MuZero-based algorithms&nbsp;<cite cl=
ass=3D"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(Schrittwieser et&nbsp;al., <a class=
=3D"ltx_ref" href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2405.11778v1#bib.bib42" title=
=3D"">2020</a>; Hubert et&nbsp;al., <a class=3D"ltx_ref" href=3D"https://ar=
xiv.org/html/2405.11778v1#bib.bib21" title=3D"">2021</a>; Antonoglou et&nbs=
p;al., <a class=3D"ltx_ref" href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2405.11778v1#bib=
.bib3" title=3D"">2021</a>; Ye et&nbsp;al., <a class=3D"ltx_ref" href=3D"ht=
tps://arxiv.org/html/2405.11778v1#bib.bib60" title=3D"">2021</a>; Mei et&nb=
sp;al., <a class=3D"ltx_ref" href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2405.11778v1#bi=
b.bib33" title=3D"">2022</a>)</cite> combine Monte-Carlo Tree Search (MCTS)=
, TD-MPC&nbsp;<cite class=3D"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(Hansen et&nbsp;=
al., <a class=3D"ltx_ref" href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2405.11778v1#bib.b=
ib16" title=3D"">2022</a>)</cite> integrates Model Predictive Control (MPC)=
, and ReBeL&nbsp;<cite class=3D"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(Brown et&nbs=
p;al., <a class=3D"ltx_ref" href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2405.11778v1#bib=
.bib7" title=3D"">2020</a>)</cite> incorporate a fusion of Counterfactual R=
egret Minimization (CFR). Nevertheless, the prevailing approach among these=
 algorithms typically involves treating the planning results as targets and=
 subsequently employing behavior cloning to enable the RL network to emulat=
e these targets. Muesli&nbsp;<cite class=3D"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(=
Hessel et&nbsp;al., <a class=3D"ltx_ref" href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/240=
5.11778v1#bib.bib19" title=3D"">2021</a>)</cite> first combines regularized=
 policy optimization with model learning as an auxiliary loss within the Mu=
Zero framework. However, it focuses solely on the policy gradient loss whil=
e neglecting the potential advantages of planning. Consequently, it attains=
 at most a performance level equivalent to that of MuZero. To the best of o=
ur knowledge, we are the first to combined policy gradient and MCTS plannin=
g to accurate policy learning in model-based reinforcement learning.</p><bu=
tton class=3D"sr-only button" style=3D"display: none;">Report issue for pre=
ceding element</button>
</div>
</section>
<section class=3D"ltx_paragraph" id=3D"A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3">
<h5 class=3D"ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Variants of MuZero-based algori=
thms</h5><button class=3D"sr-only button" style=3D"display: none;">Report i=
ssue for preceding element</button>
<div class=3D"ltx_para ltx_noindent" id=3D"A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1">
<p class=3D"ltx_p" id=3D"A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1">While the original MuZero al=
gorithm&nbsp;<cite class=3D"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(Schrittwieser et=
&nbsp;al., <a class=3D"ltx_ref" href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2405.11778v1=
#bib.bib42" title=3D"">2020</a>)</cite> has achieved superhuman performance=
 levels in Go and Atari, it is important to note that it harbors several li=
mitations. To address and overcome these limitations, subsequent advancemen=
ts have been made in the field. EfficientZero&nbsp;<cite class=3D"ltx_cite =
ltx_citemacro_citep">(Ye et&nbsp;al., <a class=3D"ltx_ref" href=3D"https://=
arxiv.org/html/2405.11778v1#bib.bib60" title=3D"">2021</a>)</cite>, for ins=
tance, introduces self-supervised consistency loss, value prefix prediction=
, and off-policy correction mechanisms to expedite and stabilize the traini=
ng process. Sampled MuZero&nbsp;<cite class=3D"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep=
">(Hubert et&nbsp;al., <a class=3D"ltx_ref" href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/=
2405.11778v1#bib.bib21" title=3D"">2021</a>)</cite> extends its capabilitie=
s to complex action spaces through the incorporation of sample-based policy=
 iteration. Gumbel MuZero&nbsp;<cite class=3D"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"=
>(Danihelka et&nbsp;al., <a class=3D"ltx_ref" href=3D"https://arxiv.org/htm=
l/2405.11778v1#bib.bib9" title=3D"">2021</a>)</cite> leverages the Gumbel-T=
op-k trick and modifies the planning process using Sequential Halving, ther=
eby reducing the demands of MCTS simulations. SpeedyZero&nbsp;<cite class=
=3D"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(Mei et&nbsp;al., <a class=3D"ltx_ref" hr=
ef=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2405.11778v1#bib.bib33" title=3D"">2022</a>)</=
cite> integrates a distributed RL framework to facilitate parallel training=
, further enhancing training efficiency. <cite class=3D"ltx_cite ltx_citema=
cro_citet">He et&nbsp;al. (<a class=3D"ltx_ref" href=3D"https://arxiv.org/h=
tml/2405.11778v1#bib.bib17" title=3D"">2023</a>)</cite> demonstrate that th=
e model acquired by MuZero typically lacks accuracy when employed for polic=
y evaluation, rendering it ineffective in generalizing to assess previously=
 unseen policies.</p><button class=3D"sr-only button" style=3D"display: non=
e;">Report issue for preceding element</button>
</div>
</section>
<section class=3D"ltx_paragraph" id=3D"A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4">
<h5 class=3D"ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Multi-agent reinforcement learn=
ing</h5><button class=3D"sr-only button" style=3D"display: none;">Report is=
sue for preceding element</button>
<div class=3D"ltx_para ltx_noindent" id=3D"A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1">
<p class=3D"ltx_p" id=3D"A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1">The typical approach for MAR=
L in cooperative settings involves centralized training and decentralized e=
xecution (CTDE). During the training phase, this approach leverages global =
or communication information, while during the execution phase, it restrict=
s itself to the observation information relevant to the current agent. This=
 paradigm encompasses both value-based&nbsp;<cite class=3D"ltx_cite ltx_cit=
emacro_citep">(Sunehag et&nbsp;al., <a class=3D"ltx_ref" href=3D"https://ar=
xiv.org/html/2405.11778v1#bib.bib48" title=3D"">2017</a>; Rashid et&nbsp;al=
., <a class=3D"ltx_ref" href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2405.11778v1#bib.bib=
39" title=3D"">2020</a>; Son et&nbsp;al., <a class=3D"ltx_ref" href=3D"http=
s://arxiv.org/html/2405.11778v1#bib.bib46" title=3D"">2019</a>; Yang et&nbs=
p;al., <a class=3D"ltx_ref" href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2405.11778v1#bib=
.bib57" title=3D"">2020</a>; Wang et&nbsp;al., <a class=3D"ltx_ref" href=3D=
"https://arxiv.org/html/2405.11778v1#bib.bib52" title=3D"">2020a</a>)</cite=
> and policy-based&nbsp;<cite class=3D"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(Lowe =
et&nbsp;al., <a class=3D"ltx_ref" href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2405.11778=
v1#bib.bib31" title=3D"">2017</a>; Liu et&nbsp;al., <a class=3D"ltx_ref" hr=
ef=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2405.11778v1#bib.bib29" title=3D"">2020</a>; P=
eng et&nbsp;al., <a class=3D"ltx_ref" href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2405.1=
1778v1#bib.bib38" title=3D"">2021</a>; Ryu et&nbsp;al., <a class=3D"ltx_ref=
" href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2405.11778v1#bib.bib40" title=3D"">2020</a=
>; Ye et&nbsp;al., <a class=3D"ltx_ref" href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2405=
.11778v1#bib.bib59" title=3D"">2023</a>)</cite> MARL methods within the con=
text of model-free scenarios. Model-based MARL algorithms remains relativel=
y underexplored with only a few methods as follows: MAMBPO&nbsp;<cite class=
=3D"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(Willemsen et&nbsp;al., <a class=3D"ltx_r=
ef" href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2405.11778v1#bib.bib56" title=3D"">2021<=
/a>)</cite> pioneers the fusion of the CTDE framework with Dyan-style model=
-based techniques, emphasizing the utilization of generated data closely re=
sembling real-world data. CPS&nbsp;<cite class=3D"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_ci=
tep">(Bargiacchi et&nbsp;al., <a class=3D"ltx_ref" href=3D"https://arxiv.or=
g/html/2405.11778v1#bib.bib6" title=3D"">2021</a>)</cite> introduces dynami=
c and reward models to determine data priorities based on the MAMBPO approa=
ch. Tesseract&nbsp;<cite class=3D"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(Mahajan et=
&nbsp;al., <a class=3D"ltx_ref" href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2405.11778v1=
#bib.bib32" title=3D"">2021</a>)</cite> dissects states and actions into lo=
w-rank tensors and evaluates the Q function using Dynamic Programming (DP) =
within an approximate environment model. MAMBA&nbsp;<cite class=3D"ltx_cite=
 ltx_citemacro_citep">(Egorov &amp; Shpilman, <a class=3D"ltx_ref" href=3D"=
https://arxiv.org/html/2405.11778v1#bib.bib10" title=3D"">2022</a>)</cite> =
incorporates the word model proposed in DreamerV2&nbsp;<cite class=3D"ltx_c=
ite ltx_citemacro_citep">(Hafner et&nbsp;al., <a class=3D"ltx_ref" href=3D"=
https://arxiv.org/html/2405.11778v1#bib.bib14" title=3D"">2020</a>)</cite> =
and introduces an attention mechanism to facilitate communication. This int=
egration leads to noteworthy performance improvements and a substantial enh=
ancement in sample efficiency when compared to previous model-free methods.=
 To the best of our knowledge, we are the first to expand the MuZero framew=
ork and incorporate MCTS planning into the context of model-based MARL sett=
ings.</p><button class=3D"sr-only button" style=3D"display: none;">Report i=
ssue for preceding element</button>
</div>
</section>
</section>
