<section class=3D"ltx_subsection" id=3D"A2.SS2">
<h3 class=3D"ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">
<span class=3D"ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Training Details</h3>=
<button class=3D"sr-only button" style=3D"display: none;">Report issue for =
preceding element</button>
<div class=3D"ltx_para ltx_noindent" id=3D"A2.SS2.p1">
<p class=3D"ltx_p" id=3D"A2.SS2.p1.1">MAZero employs a similar pipeline to =
EfficientZero&nbsp;<cite class=3D"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(Ye et&nbsp=
;al., <a class=3D"ltx_ref" href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2405.11778v1#bib.=
bib60" title=3D"">2021</a>)</cite> while asynchronizing the parallel stages=
 of data collection (Self-play workers), reanalysis (Reanalyze workers), an=
d training (Main Thread) to maintain the reproducibility of the same random=
 seed.</p><button class=3D"sr-only button" style=3D"display: none;">Report =
issue for preceding element</button>
</div>
<div class=3D"ltx_para ltx_noindent" id=3D"A2.SS2.p2">
<p class=3D"ltx_p" id=3D"A2.SS2.p2.1">We use the Adam optimizer&nbsp;<cite =
class=3D"ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(Kingma &amp; Ba, <a class=3D"ltx_re=
f" href=3D"https://arxiv.org/html/2405.11778v1#bib.bib24" title=3D"">2014</=
a>)</cite> for training, with a batch size of 256 and a constant learning r=
ate of <math alttext=3D"10^{-4}" class=3D"ltx_Math" display=3D"inline" id=
=3D"A2.SS2.p2.1.m1.1"><semantics id=3D"A2.SS2.p2.1.m1.1a"><msup id=3D"A2.SS=
2.p2.1.m1.1.1" xref=3D"A2.SS2.p2.1.m1.1.1.cmml"><mn id=3D"A2.SS2.p2.1.m1.1.=
1.2" xref=3D"A2.SS2.p2.1.m1.1.1.2.cmml">10</mn><mrow id=3D"A2.SS2.p2.1.m1.1=
.1.3" xref=3D"A2.SS2.p2.1.m1.1.1.3.cmml"><mo id=3D"A2.SS2.p2.1.m1.1.1.3a" x=
ref=3D"A2.SS2.p2.1.m1.1.1.3.cmml">=E2=88=92</mo><mn id=3D"A2.SS2.p2.1.m1.1.=
1.3.2" xref=3D"A2.SS2.p2.1.m1.1.1.3.2.cmml">4</mn></mrow></msup><annotation=
-xml encoding=3D"MathML-Content" id=3D"A2.SS2.p2.1.m1.1b"><apply id=3D"A2.S=
